        <h2 id="comparison">Quick Comparison: 10 Supplier Profiles at a Glance</h2>
        <p>Scan this table by scenario, not by rank. "Best For" is the column that matters.</p>
        <div class="ar-table-wrap"><table class="ar-table"><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Supplier Profile</th><th>Fabric Focus</th><th>Typical MOQ</th><th>Sampling</th><th>Certifications</th><th>Lead Time (prod. + sea)</th><th>Best For</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Heavyweight specialist</td><td>380–500 GSM fleece</td><td>300–500 pcs/color</td><td>7–14 days</td><td>OEKO-TEX, BSCI</td><td>35–50 + 25–35 days</td><td>Premium heavyweight brands</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Low-MOQ custom house</td><td>280–380 GSM</td><td>50–150 pcs/color</td><td>5–10 days</td><td>OEKO-TEX</td><td>25–40 + 25–35 days</td><td>New brands, test orders</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Organic cotton mill</td><td>300–420 GSM organic</td><td>500–1,000 pcs/color</td><td>10–15 days</td><td>GOTS, OEKO-TEX</td><td>40–55 + 25–35 days</td><td>Sustainable DTC labels</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Large-volume exporter</td><td>280–450 GSM</td><td>1,000–3,000 pcs/style</td><td>10–15 days</td><td>BSCI, WRAP, ISO 9001</td><td>30–45 + 25–35 days</td><td>Wholesale, retail programs</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Full-package OEM/ODM</td><td>280–450 GSM</td><td>300–800 pcs/style</td><td>10–20 days</td><td>OEKO-TEX, BSCI</td><td>35–50 + 25–35 days</td><td>Brands wanting turnkey</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Print &amp; embroidery studio</td><td>280–400 GSM</td><td>100–300 pcs/design</td><td>5–12 days</td><td>OEKO-TEX</td><td>25–40 + 25–35 days</td><td>Graphic-heavy streetwear</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Fast-sampling workshop</td><td>280–380 GSM</td><td>50–200 pcs/color</td><td>3–7 days</td><td>OEKO-TEX</td><td>20–35 + 25–35 days</td><td>Time-sensitive launches</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Budget bulk producer</td><td>260–350 GSM</td><td>1,000–5,000 pcs/style</td><td>10–15 days</td><td>BSCI</td><td>30–45 + 25–35 days</td><td>Price-sensitive volume</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Premium streetwear partner</td><td>400–500 GSM</td><td>200–500 pcs/color</td><td>10–18 days</td><td>OEKO-TEX, BSCI</td><td>35–50 + 25–35 days</td><td>Designer streetwear</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Full-service sourcing &amp; QC</td><td>Varies by partner</td><td>200–1,000 pcs/style</td><td>7–15 days</td><td>Varies by partner</td><td>30–50 + 25–35 days</td><td>Buyers managing complexity</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
        <p class="ar-note"><em>All figures reflect typical industry ranges for 100% cotton hoodies. Confirm current MOQ, pricing, and lead times directly with each supplier.</em></p>
        <p><strong>Before you contact anyone, write down:</strong> target GSM, order quantity per color, decoration type, target landed cost, and launch date. Suppliers quote faster and more accurately when you lead with numbers.</p>
        <h2 id="profiles">The 10 Chinese Hoodie Supplier Profiles (and Which Fits Your Order)</h2>
        <p>We describe supplier archetypes rather than naming companies, because the useful question isn't "what's the name," it's "does this type of factory match my order." Identify your archetype, then run individual candidates through the methodology above.</p>
        <h3>1. Heavyweight Specialist: Best for 400+ GSM Cotton Hoodies</h3>
        <p>Built around 380–500 GSM fleece and french terry in combed ring-spun 20s–24s yarn, with pre-shrunk fabric and documented dimensional stability. Garment wash (vintage, acid, mineral) is the strongest customization; print and embroidery are available but secondary. <strong>Best for:</strong> premium brands where weight and hand-feel carry the product. Wrong fit for 50-piece runs or rock-bottom pricing.</p>
        <h3>2. Low-MOQ Custom House: Best for Small-Batch Orders</h3>
        <p>Mid-weight cotton fleece with full print, embroidery, custom labels, and custom packaging. Quality holds up well for the tier, though heavyweight options above 400 GSM are thin on the ground, and audit certifications beyond OEKO-TEX are uncommon at this scale. <strong>Best for:</strong> new DTC brands and Shopify sellers validating a design before committing cash to volume.</p>
        <h3>3. Organic Cotton Mill: Best for GOTS-Certified Cotton</h3>
        <p>GOTS-certified organic fleece with organic-certified trims and dyes. Fiber-to-garment traceability is the real differentiator, not the hand-feel. Confirm the GOTS transaction certificate covers your specific order rather than only the facility; that distinction trips up more buyers than any other certification issue. More detail in our notes on <a href="/our-services/">GOTS-certified organic cotton sourcing</a>. <strong>Best for:</strong> eco-positioned brands selling into markets where organic claims face regulatory scrutiny.</p>
        <h3>4. Large-Volume Exporter: Best for Bulk Export Programs</h3>
        <p>Broad GSM range with consistent output across runs of several thousand units, typically backed by BSCI, WRAP, and ISO 9001 (verify each one). Decoration and labeling stay standard; experimental finishes are rarely accommodated at this scale. <strong>Best for:</strong> wholesalers and brands with repeatable volume who weight reliability and unit cost above flexibility.</p>
        <h3>5. Full-Package OEM/ODM: Best for Turnkey Development</h3>
        <p>Cotton fleece and french terry across the common mid-weight bands, with in-house pattern-making, grading, trim development, branding, and packaging under one roof. <strong>Best for:</strong> brands that want one partner to carry a concept to finished goods without juggling three vendors and a freight forwarder.</p>
